     <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
     <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
     <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+
+    <p><strong>Reading list</strong></p>
+    <p>Your reading list is stored server-side in a session identified by a strictly necessary cookie. It contains only article identifiers, is limited to 100 entries, and is not linked to any other personal data.</p>
+
+    <p><strong>Analytics</strong></p>
+    <p>Anonymous usage analytics are loaded from a third-party host only if you click “Allow analytics”. Nothing is requested from the analytics provider before that. Your choice is stored in your browser (local storage) and can be changed at any time via “Manage Privacy Preferences” in the footer. We treat Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track signals as a refusal.</p>
+
+    <h2>4. Third-party services</h2>
+    <p><strong>Google Fonts</strong> serves the headline typeface; your IP address is transmitted to Google when it loads.</p>
+    <p><strong>Account service</strong> (hosted on Google Cloud Functions) receives the username and password you enter on the sign-in and sign-up pages. Requests are sent without cookies and without a referrer. Passwords are never stored in your browser.</p>
+    <p>All third-party services are listed, with the data they receive, in our internal register, which is reviewed regularly (see below).</p>
+
+    <h2>5. Security and retention</h2>
+    <p>The site is served over HTTPS only and uses security headers (Content Security Policy, HSTS, frame and referrer restrictions) to limit data exposure. Session data is kept only as long as needed to provide the reading list.</p>
+
+    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
+    <p>You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal data and withdraw consent at any time.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
